# Logs
#
# `/logs` is ANCHORED, deliberately. Unanchored it matches a directory named
# `logs` at any depth — and this tree has LogPane.tsx, logFilters.ts and a
# whole log-viewing surface, so `src/components/run/logs/` is a plausible
# next directory. That is exactly how a bare `lib/` in the root .gitignore
# silently kept `frontend/src/lib` — the entire wire contract — out of two
# commits. `git add -A` says nothing when a path is ignored.
/logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
bun-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules

# The build output is not in this directory. `vite.config.ts` writes `../dist`
# — the repo root, which is also the APP root: `resources/app.yml` hands that
# folder to Databricks Apps, and `app/spa.py` serves the bundle out of it.
# This tree is the client SOURCE, and `databricks.yml` excludes all of it.
#
# That `dist/` is COMMITTED, which is unusual and deliberate. Deploying from
# inside Databricks — a Git folder, a notebook — there is no Node runtime and
# only git-tracked files exist, so a gitignored bundle would simply not be
# there and every page would answer 503 while the API worked fine. Committing
# it is the only route the SPA has into a workspace-driven deploy.
#
# The cost is real: **rebuild and commit dist whenever the frontend changes**,
# or the deployed UI is silently stale.
#
# Sourcemaps stay out. `vite.config.ts` sets `sourcemap: true` and they are
# 5.1 MB against 1.2 MB for the bundle itself — worth having locally, not
# worth a fresh copy in git on every frontend change. The root .gitignore
# carries that rule, next to the tracked directory it applies to.
dist-ssr
*.local

# `vite.config.ts` configures an html coverage reporter, and vitest writes it
# to ./coverage. Nothing ignored it, so `vitest run --coverage` left an
# untracked directory in a shared tree. databricks.yml already excludes
# `frontend/coverage/**` from the workspace sync; this is the other half.
coverage

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?
